                  <provenance type="#m s"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_295">Lanthony (secunda),
                        Gloucestershire. Augustinian priory of St Mary the Virgin and St John the
                        Baptist</orgName><p>Lambeth Palace 425, fols. i, 1–21, and 431, fols. i,
                        1–7, 16–88, formed one volume, earlier at Llanthony, q.v.; script,
                        contents, and the medieval table of contents (Lambeth 431, fol. 87v) show
                        that Lambeth 425 fols. 1–21 followed 431 fol. 65.</p><p>applying to it the
                        note: </p><p>London, BL, Royal MS 2 C. x; Lambeth Palace 30; 80, fols. 168–244;
                        101; 138, fols. 1–44; 148; 153, fols. 156–179; 165, fols. 102–190; 195;
                        200, fols. 114–163; 208; 215; 218, fols. 1–89; 227; 231; 345, fols.
                        97–227; 360, fols. 1–118; 365, fols. 1–119; 377; 378, fols. i, ii, 1–56,
                        125–165; 390; 394; 397; 398; 409; 449; 452; 481; Oxford, Bodl. Bodley 839,
                        Hatton 49, Corpus Christi Coll. 33, 43; Trinity Coll. 39 have a note of
                        contents in the hand of 'Morganus canonicus de Kermerden' (s. xv), who has
                        written his name in many of the books.</p><p> </p><p> </p><p> </p><p> </p></provenance>
               </history>
