                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="org_327">Llanthony (prima),
                        Monmouthshire. Augustinian priory of St John the Baptist; cell of Lanthony
                        (secunda) from AD 1481</orgName><p>The catalogue in MS. Tanner 268 (L.Θ.1)
                        shows that this was bound with MS. 431, fols. i, 1–7, 16–88 in s. xvii, as
                        L.Θ.1 (K. 16). </p><p>Marginalia etc. show that Lambeth Palace 425, fols.
                        1–21, and 431, fols. i, 1–7, 16–88 formed one volume.</p></provenance>
